  data: {
    LLM: 'Dealer leads by placing one covered tile and one face-up attack tile. On each subsequent turn, a player may pass or respond by playing a matching tile (or a king except against lance/pawn), then immediately plays a new attack tile. If three consecutive players pass, the last successful attacker leads again with a covered tile and any new attack. Players always act by either playing two tiles or passing. The deal ends when a player plays their final pair.',
    Player: 'Dealer leads by placing one covered tile and one face-up attack tile. On each subsequent turn, a player may pass or respond by playing a matching tile (or a king except against lance/pawn), then immediately plays a new attack tile. If three consecutive players pass, the last successful attacker leads again with a covered tile and any new attack. Players always act by either playing two tiles or passing. The deal ends when a player plays their final pair.',
    objective: 'Empty your hand first so your team scores the value of your final attack tile and reaches game target before opponents.',
    gameplay: 'Dealer leads by placing one covered tile and one face-up attack tile. On each subsequent turn, a player may pass or respond by playing a matching tile (or a king except against lance/pawn), then immediately plays a new attack tile. If three consecutive players pass, the last successful attacker leads again with a covered tile and any new attack. Players always act by either playing two tiles or passing. The deal ends when a player plays their final pair.',
    keyRules: [
      'Kings can substitute only against non-lance and non-pawn attacks.',
      'Passing is always allowed, even when a legal response exists.',
      'A king cannot be used as an attack unless the other king is already face up or both kings are in your hand.',
      'Special pre-play pawn holdings (five or more) can trigger immediate win/redeal outcomes.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
