    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 8 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Empty your hand first so your team scores the value of your final attack tile and reaches game target before opponents.',
      'Turn-flow example: Dealer leads by placing one covered tile and one face-up attack tile. On each subsequent turn, a player may pass or respond by playing a matching tile (or a king except against lance/pawn), then immediately plays a new attack tile. If three consecutive players pass, the last successful attacker leads again with a covered tile and any new attack. Players always act by either playing two tiles or passing. The deal ends when a player plays their final pair.',
      "Scoring example: Winning team scores the point value of the winner's final attack tile; some finishes after triple-pass allow doubled value when final pair is equal. First partnership to reach 150 cumulative points wins..",
